        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "225d647a-902b-5821-828c-dd2853ae97cd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: HMS Calpe (L71), Type II Hunt-class destroyer escort\n- Organizations: Royal Navy, Allied forces\n- Events: World War II, Dieppe Raid, Battle of Dieppe, Operation Rutter, Operation Jubilee\n- Places: Dieppe, northern coast of France\n\nFacts:\n- HMS Calpe (L71) was built as a result of the outbreak of World War II.\n- HMS Calpe (L71) was a British Royal Navy Type II Hunt-class destroyer escort.\n- HMS Calpe (L71) escorted convoys during World War II and participated in the Dieppe Raid.\n- The Dieppe Raid was also known as the Battle of Dieppe, Operation Rutter during planning, and Operation Jubilee as its final official code name.\n- The Dieppe Raid was an Allied attack on the German-occupied port of Dieppe during the Second World War.\n- The Dieppe Raid took place on the northern coast of France on 19 August 1942.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
